3:["$","p","Narrower 1-inch slats create a more refi",{"children":"Narrower 1-inch slats create a more refined, traditional look and work well on smaller windows. They provide more precise light control due to the greater number of slats per window."}]
4:["$","p","Wider 2-inch and 2.5-inch slats offer a ",{"children":"Wider 2-inch and 2.5-inch slats offer a bolder, more contemporary appearance and allow a clearer view when open. They also collect less dust per unit area and are easier to clean. For large windows, wider slats maintain better proportions."}]
5:["$","div","2",{"className":"flex flex-col items-start","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[18px] font-semibold leading-[27px] tracking-[-0.0648px] text-navy","children":"3. Finishes and Customization"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy","children":[["$","p","Wood blinds offer extensive customizatio",{"children":"Wood blinds offer extensive customization options. Stains range from light natural tones to deep espresso, and painted finishes in white, ivory, or custom colors complement any interior design scheme."}],["$","p","Decorative tapes — fabric strips that co",{"children":"Decorative tapes — fabric strips that cover the ladder cords — add a design element and come in dozens of colors and patterns. They also hide the small holes where the lift cords pass through each slat."}],["$","p","Valances, cornices, and holdbacks provid",{"children":"Valances, cornices, and holdbacks provide finishing touches. A contoured or crown valance gives a polished, furniture-like appearance that elevates the entire window treatment."}]]}]]}]
6:["$","div","3",{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 md:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","div","Side-by-side comparison of real wood and faux wood blinds",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-1.webp","alt":"Side-by-side comparison of real wood and faux wood blinds","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}],["$","div","Different slat widths displayed on adjacent windows",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-2.webp","alt":"Different slat widths displayed on adjacent windows","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}],["$","div","Decorative tape options on wooden blinds",{"className":"relative h-[240px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg md:h-[280px] xl:h-[359px]","children":["$","$L2",null,{"src":"/images/resources/knowledge-grid-3.webp","alt":"Decorative tape options on wooden blinds","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}]]}]
7:["$","div","4",{"className":"flex flex-col items-start","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[18px] font-semibold leading-[27px] tracking-[-0.0648px] text-navy","children":"4. Installation and Care Tips"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy","children":[["$","p","Proper installation is critical for wood",{"children":"Proper installation is critical for wooden blinds. Ensure your window frame has sufficient depth for inside mounting — most wood blinds require at least 2.75 inches. Verify that the frame is square and level before drilling."}],["$","p","For ongoing care, dust regularly with a ",{"children":"For ongoing care, dust regularly with a soft cloth or blind-specific duster. Avoid water on real wood — use a wood-safe cleaner applied to the cloth, not directly to the blinds. Faux wood can handle a damp cloth for heavier cleaning."}],["$","p","If real wood blinds begin to show signs ",{"children":"If real wood blinds begin to show signs of humidity damage (warping or discoloration), consider moving them to a drier room and replacing them with faux wood in the humid location. Early intervention prevents further damage."}]]}]]}]
